**Re-check the context before installing an acquired slot.**

`acquire()` checks lifecycle state at line 86, then awaits filesystem work (lines 90-107). `close()` does not wait for pending acquisitions. It checks only tracked child processes, sets `retired`, and closes the slots already registered. If `close()` runs during that await, `acquire()` still installs the slot at line 110 without another lifecycle check. The slot is then held. `close()` will not release it, and later `close()` calls reject the retired context.

Add a lifecycle check immediately before the slot is installed. If the context retired during the await, the existing `catch` closes the slot and rethrows.

